  "description": "Microsoft's DirectX 8 for Visual Basic (dx8vb.dll, version 5.03.2600.2180 from Windows XP SP2), registered once for every game that needs it. Many Visual Basic 6 audio games use it for sound and input; Windows Vista and later don't include it, and those games then stop with \"Class not registered\" or a missing dx8vb.dll.\n\nMicrosoft no longer offers a download with this file, so it comes from Aprone's Community Feud download, which ships this exact build; everything else in that archive is removed before it is registered.",
